+## Bulk import
+
+`importTasks(list, text)` adds many tasks at once, for teams moving their lists over from spreadsheets. The
+text holds one task per line, written `title;priority;tags`:
+
+- the priority may be left empty for a normal one;
+- the tags are separated by spaces.
+
+For example:
+
+```
+Renew the insurance;high;admin money
+Sweep the porch;;home
+```
+
+Blank lines are skipped. Each valid line is added to the list, and the function returns
+`{ imported, rejected }`: `imported` is how many tasks were added, and `rejected` lists every line that could
+not be added as `{ line, reason }`, with `line` counting from 1 (blank lines included). A line is rejected when
+it does not have exactly three `;`-separated fields, or when its title, priority or tags are not valid, or when
+its title is already in the list. Rejected lines do not stop the others from being added. Lines may end in LF or
+CRLF.
+
 Run its tests with `npm test`.
